# Tasks declared by row rather than by an (npc-task ..) head: duties an org assigns
# (org_duties, tables/duty-tables.mc) that no rule performs yet. A duty is a TASK label -
# {@self duty-to ?org [k <duty>]} - so the name is a task term under act > task.
relation
    act (noun)
        task (noun) (+ task) (+ sub [k human] @object)
            dismiss_staff
            review_staff
            keep_records
            provide_for
            protect
            officiate
            admit_member
